# 7. CRITICAL MAP BUG FIX

There is an existing problem where the map displays the same location even after the user changes pickup or destination.

This must be properly investigated and fixed.

Do not simply update the text input while keeping old coordinates.

## Required behaviour

Whenever a user changes pickup or destination:

1. Read the latest selected location.
2. Geocode the new location.
3. Obtain the correct latitude and longitude.
4. Update the pickup marker.
5. Update the destination marker.
6. Recalculate the route.
7. Update the distance.
8. Update the estimated delivery time.
9. Recalculate the delivery price.

The map must always reflect the latest selected locations.

## Technical requirements

Inspect the existing map implementation.

Check for:
- Incorrect React state.
- Stale location values.
- Incorrect geocoding.
- Cached coordinates.
- React Leaflet marker update problems.
- Incorrect map component rendering.
- Asynchronous request race conditions.

Implement proper state management.

Maintain separate state for:

pickupLocation
pickupLatitude
pickupLongitude
destinationLocation
destinationLatitude
destinationLongitude

Ensure markers update when their coordinates change.

Use correct React keys and update marker positions properly.

Prevent outdated geocoding responses from overwriting newer selections.

Recalculate the route whenever either endpoint changes.

Allow users to swap pickup and destination.

Provide loading indicators while resolving locations.

Display an error when a location cannot be found.

Use OpenStreetMap-compatible geocoding and routing services.

Do not require paid Google Maps APIs.

Allow manual map pin selection as a fallback.

